    "stable_id": "euclid-backward-construction",
    "canonical_statement": "For all positive integers m and n with m > n, gcd(m,n) = 1, and m and n of opposite parity, if a = m^2 - n^2, b = 2mn, and c = m^2 + n^2, then a, b, c are positive integers satisfying a^2 + b^2 = c^2 and gcd(a,b,c) = 1.",
